  "configuration_id": "config_044",
  "reason": "The current best (config_035: scvi_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) achieves 0.725 accuracy. All six completed experiments use scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, so the RNA encoder choice is the most important untested variable in the best-performing architecture context. config_044 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) directly tests whether a different learned RNA representation (scgpt, a generative model vs. scvi's variational model) can improve on 0.725 while keeping the proven-best image encoder, aggregation, and fusion. This is the highest-information experiment: if scgpt wins, we've found a new best and can exploit it in remaining experiments; if it loses, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can focus remaining budget on minor refinements. Expected cost is moderate (~4-6 GPU hours), comparable to config_003 (4.65 h) and config_035 (3.60 h), since scgpt and scvi_n200 are both learned encoders of similar scale paired with ViT-L and transformer aggregation."
}

